## 4. USER ROLES AND PERMISSIONS

Implement four user roles.

### ROLE 1: RESEARCHER / PROPONENT

Researchers are external users who submit proposals for research funding.

Permissions:
- Register an account.
- Log in and log out.
- Manage their personal profile.
- View available funding opportunities.
- Create research proposals.
- Save proposals as drafts.
- Edit their own drafts.
- Upload proposal documents.
- Submit proposals.
- View their submitted proposals.
- Track proposal status.
- View evaluation feedback and administrative remarks when released.
- View their approved projects.
- Submit project progress reports.
- View project history.

Researchers must never be allowed to approve their own proposals or access another researcher's private submissions.

### ROLE 2: ADMINISTRATOR

Administrators manage the overall application.

Permissions:
- View all users.
- View all researchers.
- Manage user accounts.
- Activate or deactivate accounts.
- View all submitted proposals.
- Perform administrative completeness checks.
- Return incomplete submissions for correction.
- Assign proposals to evaluators.
- View evaluation results.
- Record final approval or disapproval decisions.
- Manage funding opportunities.
- Manage projects.
- View all reports.
- View system statistics.
- View audit logs.

### ROLE 3: EVALUATOR

Evaluators review assigned research proposals.

Permissions:
- View proposals assigned to them.
- View proposal information.
- View uploaded documents.
- Evaluate assigned proposals.
- Provide scores.
- Write evaluation remarks.
- Submit recommendations.
- View their evaluation history.

Evaluators must not be able to manage user accounts or approve funding independently.

### ROLE 4: PROJECT OFFICER / MONITORING PERSONNEL

Project officers monitor approved projects.

Permissions:
- View approved and ongoing projects.
- View project information.
- Update monitoring status.
- Review progress reports.
- Record monitoring remarks.
- Track project timelines.
- View project accomplishments.
- Mark projects as completed, subject to authorized approval.

