## 10. PROPOSAL WORKFLOW AND STATUS MANAGEMENT

Implement the following simplified workflow:

Draft
↓
Submitted
↓
Administrative Review
↓
For Correction (if incomplete)
↓
Under Evaluation
↓
For Approval
↓
Approved / Disapproved

If approved:
↓
Project Created
↓
Ongoing
↓
For Monitoring
↓
Completed

Important business rules:

- Researchers can only edit drafts and proposals explicitly returned for correction.
- Only administrators can perform administrative review and final decisions.
- Evaluators can only evaluate proposals assigned to them.
- A proposal cannot be approved without a completed evaluation.
- A submitted proposal cannot be silently edited.
- Every status change must be saved in the status history.
- Every important action must record the responsible user and timestamp.
- An approved proposal must create a corresponding project record.
- Disapproved proposals must remain accessible for historical records.
- A project cannot be completed without an appropriate final monitoring decision.

