## 13. SECURITY AND VALIDATION

Implement:
- Laravel CSRF protection.
- Server-side input validation.
- Password hashing.
- Role-based middleware.
- Authorization checks on every protected action.
- Secure session handling.
- File type and size validation.
- Unique tracking numbers.
- Protected document access.
- Audit logs.
- Environment-based Firebase credentials.

Never trust role values or user IDs submitted from the browser.

Because Laravel accesses Firestore using privileged service credentials, do not rely solely on Firestore Security Rules. Enforce access permissions in Laravel controllers, services, and policies.

